      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_23",
        on: "branch_if_23",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "unit.id",
            equals: "Krawg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Krawg",
            text: _("Screech!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_24",
        on: "branch_if_24",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "unit.id",
            equals: "Krawg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Krawg saw that this tablet was like the others held by the orc and troll, and knew that this could remove the last bridge across the fire lake."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Yes, Krawg, that must be the last rune sealing the volcano. Smash it, like the others!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Krawg",
            text: _("Krawg sad."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Just do it, you dumb bird! You can escape, our enemies cannot. We knew that death was likely when we fled here, just go!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Wait! If Krawg can escape, shouldn’t we give him the Sceptre?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("No, too risky, even if Krawg drops it in King Haldric’s hand. You’ve seen how the elves have behaved, you’ve seen how your lord behaved. The corrupting emissions from the ruby are nothing compared to the greed already out there, and my crafted gold cage does nothing to contain that."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Durstorn and Glildur have both convinced me that the time is not right for the Sceptre of Fire, best that it rests with us for a while. Now, Krawg!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Krawg",
            text: _("Yah! Krah!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_25",
        on: "branch_if_25",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "unit.id",
            not_equals: "Krawg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "$unit.id",
            text: _("There’s a tablet with a rune here!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Yes, that must be the last rune sealing the volcano. Smash it, like the others!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "$unit.id",
            text: _("The resulting eruption will lead to all of your deaths!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Just do it! You riders have a chance to escape, our enemies cannot. We knew that death was likely when we fled here, just go!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Wait! If the riders can escape, shouldn’t we give them the Sceptre?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("No, too risky, even if they drop it in King Haldric’s hand. You’ve seen how the elves have behaved, you’ve seen how your lord behaved. The corrupting emissions from the ruby are nothing compared to the greed already out there, and my crafted gold cage does nothing to contain that."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Thursagan",
            text: _("Durstorn and Glildur have both convinced me that the time is not right for the Sceptre of Fire, best that it rests with us for a while. Now, smash it!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "$unit.id",
            text: _("Alright, there’s no turning back now!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_26",
        on: "branch_if_26",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "gryphonrider_flag",
            equals: "yes",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Once the magic seal capping the throat of the volcano was removed, lava and toxic gas exploded upward, killing everyone inside and sealing them in a tomb of hot, flowing rock. Krawg and the gryphon riders flew towards a hole in the roof but it was only Krawg who managed to outrun the explosion and emerge as the sole survivor. The Sceptre of Fire would wait, unharmed by the lava, until some day far in the future."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_27",
        on: "branch_if_27",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "gryphonrider_flag",
            not_equals: "yes",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
